{
  "total": 304,
  "totalPage": 7,
  "page": 3,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b319",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 249,
      "bookHadithIndex": 101,
      "text": "(Another chain) from Wa'il bin Hujr who narrated it from :the Prophet, and it is similar to the narrations of Sufyan from Salamah bin Kuhail",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-249-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-249-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b31a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 250,
      "bookHadithIndex": 102,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said \"When the Imam says 'Amin' then (all of you) say 'Amin.' For whoever's 'Amin' concurs with the 'Amin' of the angels, then his past sins will be forgiven",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-250-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-250-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-250-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-250-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b31b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 251,
      "bookHadithIndex": 103,
      "text": "Al-Hasan narrated that :Samurah said: \"there are two pauses that I preserved from Allah's Messenger.\" But Imran bin Husain rejected that and said: \"We preserved one pause.\" \"So we wrote to Ubayy bin Ka'b in Al-Madinah. Ubayy wrote that Samurah was correct.\" Sa'eed said: \"We said to Qatadah: 'What are those two pauses?' He said: 'When he entered into his Salat, and when he finished his recitation.' Then he (Qatadah) said after that: 'And when he recited (Nor those who went astray.)' And he said: 'He liked to pause when he finished the recitation until he caught his breath",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-251-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-251-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-251-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b31c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 252,
      "bookHadithIndex": 104,
      "text": "Qabisah bin Hulb narrated from :his father who said: \"Allah's Messenger lead us in prayer and hold his left hand with his right",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-252-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-252-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-252-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-252-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b31d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 253,
      "bookHadithIndex": 105,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:\"Allah's Messenger would say the Takbir for every lowering and raising, standing and sitting, and (so did) Abu Bakr and Umar",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-253-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-253-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-253-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-253-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b31e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 254,
      "bookHadithIndex": 106,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated:\"Allah's Messenger would say the Takhir while he was going down",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-254-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-254-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-254-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-254-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b31f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 255,
      "bookHadithIndex": 107,
      "text": "Salim narrated from :his father (Ibn Umar) who said: \"I saw Allah's Messenger when he opened the Salat, raising his hands to the level of his shoulders, and (again) when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing.\" In his narration, Ibn Abi Umar added: \"And he wuld not raise them between the two prostrations",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-255-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-255-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-255-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b320",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 256,
      "bookHadithIndex": 108,
      "text": "Salim narrated:Same as 255 (above) with a different chain",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-256-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-256-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-256-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-256-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b321",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 257,
      "bookHadithIndex": 109,
      "text": "Alqamah narrated that :Abdullah bin Mas'ud said: \"Shall I not demonstrate the Salat of Allah's Messenger to you?\" Then he offered Salat and he did not raise his hands except while saying the first Takbir",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-257-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-257-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-257-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b322",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 258,
      "bookHadithIndex": 110,
      "text": "Abu Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami said:\"Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] said to us: 'The knees are the Sunnah for you, so hold the knees",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-258-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-258-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-258-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-258-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b323",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 259,
      "bookHadithIndex": 111,
      "text": "Sa'd bin Abi Waqas said:\"We would do that, but then we were prohibited from it, and we were ordered to put our hands on our knees",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-259-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-259-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-259-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b324",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 260,
      "bookHadithIndex": 112,
      "text": "Abbas bin Sahl [bin Sa'd] narrated:\"Abu Humaid, Abu Usaid, Sahl bin Sa'd, and Muhammad bin Maslamah were once together and they were mentioning the Salat of Allah's Messenger. Abu Humaid said: 'I am the most knowledgeable among you of the Salat of Allah's Messenger: Allah's Messenger would bow and place his hands on his knees as if he was grasping them, and he would draw his forearms to hold them away from his sides",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-260-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-260-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-260-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-260-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b325",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 261,
      "bookHadithIndex": 113,
      "text": "Ibn Mas'ud narrated that :the Prophet said: \"When one of you bows then says while he is bowing: (Subhana Rabbiyal Azim) 'Glorious is my Lord the Magnificent' three times, then he has completed his bowing. And that is the least of it. And when he prostrates and says while prostrating: (Subhana Rabbiyal A'la) 'Glorious is my Lord the Most High' three times, then he has completed his prostrations, and that is the least of it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-261-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-261-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-261-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b326",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 262,
      "bookHadithIndex": 114,
      "text": "Hudhaifah narrated that :he performed Salat with the Prophet, and that while he was bowing he would say: (Subhana Rabbiyal Azim); \"Glorious is my Lord the Magnificent\" and while prostrating: (Subhana Rabbiyal A'la) 'Glorious is my Lord the Most High.' And he would not recite an Ayah mentioning mercy, except that he would stop and ask (for mercy), and he would not recite an Ayah mentioning punishment, except that he would stop and seek refuge (with Allah from it)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-262-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-262-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-262-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-262-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b327",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 263,
      "bookHadithIndex": 115,
      "text": "(Another similar narration) This Hadith has been narrated from Hudhaifah :from another route: \"That he performed Salat during the night with the Prophet\" and he mentioned the Hadith",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-263-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-263-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-263-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b328",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 264,
      "bookHadithIndex": 116,
      "text": "Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:\"The Prophet prohibited wearing Qassi, and that which is dyed with safflower, and from the gold ring, and from reciting the Quran while bowing",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-264-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-264-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-264-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-264-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b329",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 265,
      "bookHadithIndex": 117,
      "text": "Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari [Al-Badri] narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \"The Salat is not acceptable if a man is not at rest - meaning his back - while bowing and prostrating",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-265-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-265-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-265-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-265-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b32a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 266,
      "bookHadithIndex": 118,
      "text": "Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:\"When Allah's Messenger would raise his head from bowing he would say: (Sami Allahi liman hamidal. Rabba na lakal-hamd, mil'as-samawati wa mil'al-ardi wa mil'a ma bainahuma wa mil'a ma shi'ia min shay'in ba'd) 'Allah listens to those who praise Him. O our Lord! And to You is the praise that fills the heavens and fills the earth, and fills what is between them, and fills whatever there is beyond that You will.' He said: There are narrations on this topic from Ibn Umar, Ibn Abbas, Ibn Abi Awfa, Abu Juhaifa, and Abu Sa'eed",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-266-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-266-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-266-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-266-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b32b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 267,
      "bookHadithIndex": 119,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \"When the Imam says: (Sami Allahu liman hamidah) 'Allah listens to those who praise Him. Then (all of you) say: (Rabbana wa lakal-hamd) 'O our Lord! And to You is the praise for whoever's saying concurs with the saying of the angels, then his past sins will be forgiven",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-267-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-267-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-267-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-267-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b32c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 268,
      "bookHadithIndex": 120,
      "text": "Wa'il bin Hujr narrated:\"I saw Allah's Messenger when he prostrated placing his knees (on the ground) before his hands, and when he got up, he raised his hands before his knees",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-268-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-268-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-268-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b32d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 269,
      "bookHadithIndex": 121,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said; \"Is it that one of you intends to kneel in his Salat with the kneeling of the camel?",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-269-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-269-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-269-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b32e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 270,
      "bookHadithIndex": 122,
      "text": "Abu Humaid As-Sa'idi narrated:\"When the Prophet would prostrate, he placed his nose and his forehead on the ground, and he held his forearms away from his sides, and he placed his hands parallel to his shoulders",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-270-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-270-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-270-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-270-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b32f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 271,
      "bookHadithIndex": 123,
      "text": "Abu Ishaq narrated:\"I said to Al-Bara bin Azib: 'Where would the Prophet place his face when he prostrated?' He said: 'Between his hands",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-271-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-271-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-271-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-271-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b330",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 272,
      "bookHadithIndex": 124,
      "text": "Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib narrated that he heard :Allah's Messenger Saying: \"When the worshipper prostrates with him: His face, his hands, his knees, and his feet",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-272-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-272-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-272-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-272-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b331",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 273,
      "bookHadithIndex": 125,
      "text": "Ibn Abbas narrated:\"The Prophet ordered that one prostrate on seven bones and that he not gather his hair nor his garment",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-273-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-273-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-273-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-273-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b332",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 274,
      "bookHadithIndex": 126,
      "text": "Ubaidallah bin Abdullah bin Arqam Al-Khuza'I narrated from his father (Abdullah bin Arqam), who said:\"I was with my father at the plains of Namirah. I passed by a mount and saw Allah's Messenger standing in Salat.\" He said: \"I was looking at the earthiness of his armpits when he prostrated.\" [That is]: \"Whiteness",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-274-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-274-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-274-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b333",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 275,
      "bookHadithIndex": 127,
      "text": "Jabir narrated that :the Prophet said: \"When one of you prostrates, then let him be balanced, and let him not lay his forearms down like the lying of the dog",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-275-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-275-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-275-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-275-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b334",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 276,
      "bookHadithIndex": 128,
      "text": "Anas narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \"Be balanced in the prostration, and let one of you not spread his forearms (on the ground) in the Salat like the spreading of the dog",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-276-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-276-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-276-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-276-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b335",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 277,
      "bookHadithIndex": 129,
      "text": "Amir bin Sa'd [bin Abi Waqqas] narrated from his father:\"The Prophet ordered placing the hands (on the ground) keeping the feet erect. (by resting feet on the toes and making the tips of the toes facing the Qiblah)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-277-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-277-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b336",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 278,
      "bookHadithIndex": 130,
      "text": "(Another chain that) Amir bin Sa'd narrated:\"The Prophet ordered placing the hands (on the ground).\" And he mentioned in it: \"From his father",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-278-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-278-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-278-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b337",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 279,
      "bookHadithIndex": 131,
      "text": "Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:\"The Salat of Allah's Messenger (was such that) when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he prostrated, and when he raised his head from prostration it (all) was nearly the same",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-279-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-279-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-279-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b338",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 280,
      "bookHadithIndex": 132,
      "text": "Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:(Another chain) which is similar",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-280-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-280-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b339",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 281,
      "bookHadithIndex": 133,
      "text": "Al-Bara said:\"When we performed Salat behind Allah's Messenger, he would raise his head from bowing, and no man among us would bend his back until Allah's Messenger prostrated, then we prostrated",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-281-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-281-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-281-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-281-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b33a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 282,
      "bookHadithIndex": 134,
      "text": "Ali narrated:\"Allah's Messenger said to me: 'O Ali! I love for you what I love for myself, and I dislike for you what I dislike for myself. Do not squat between prostrations",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-282-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-282-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-282-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-282-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b33b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 283,
      "bookHadithIndex": 135,
      "text": "Tawus said:\"We asked Ibn Abbas about squatting (sitting) on the heels. He said: 'It is the Sunnah.' We said: 'We think that it is difficult for a man.' He said: 'Rather, it is Sunnah of your Prophet",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-283-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-283-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-283-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b33c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 284,
      "bookHadithIndex": 136,
      "text": "Ibn Abbas narrated:\"Between the two prostrations, the Prophet would say: (Allahummaghfir li, warhamni, wajburni, wahdini, warzuqni). 'O Allah! Pardon me, have mercy on me, help me, guide me, and grant me sustenance",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-284-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-284-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-284-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b33d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 285,
      "bookHadithIndex": 137,
      "text": "Ibn Abbas narrated:(Another chain) which is similar",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-285-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b33e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 286,
      "bookHadithIndex": 138,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated:\"[Some of] the Companions of the Prophet complained [to the Prophet] about the hardship of the prostration on them, when they were so spread out, so he said: 'Use your knees",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-286-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-286-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-286-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b33f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 287,
      "bookHadithIndex": 139,
      "text": "Malik bin Al-Huwairith Al-Laithi narrated that he saw :Allah's Messenger performing Salat. When he was in an odd number of his Salat, he would not get up until he had sat completely",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-287-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-287-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-287-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-287-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b340",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 288,
      "bookHadithIndex": 140,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated:\"Allah's Messenger would get up during his Salat on the tips of his feet",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-288-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-288-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-288-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-288-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b341",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 289,
      "bookHadithIndex": 141,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:\"Allah's Messenger taught us, that when we sit for every two Rak'ah we should say: (At-Tahyyatulillah, was-salawatu wattayybaat. As-salamu alaika ayyuhannabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu, as-salamu alaina wa ala ibadillahis-salihin. Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah wa ashadu anna Muhammadan abduhu wa Rasuluh.) 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are Allah. Peace be upon you O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and all of the righteous worshippers of Allah. I testify that nne has the right to be worshipped but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is Allah's servant and Messenger",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-289-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-289-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-289-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b342",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 290,
      "bookHadithIndex": 142,
      "text": "Ibn Abbas narrated:\"Allah's Messenger would teach us the Tashah-hud just as he would teach us the Qur'an. He would say: (At-Tahiyyatu, al mubarakatu, as-salawatu at-tayyibatulillah. Salamun alaika ayyuhan-naibiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu, salamun alaina wa ala ibadalillahis-salihin. Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah, wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan abduhu wa Raduluh.) 'All greetings, goodness, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and His blessings, Peace be upon us and all of the righteous worshippers of Allah. I testify that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is Allah's worshipper and Messenger",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-290-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-290-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-290-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-290-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b343",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 291,
      "bookHadithIndex": 143,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Mas`ud said:\"It is from the Sunnah to say the Tashahhud quietly",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-291-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-291-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-291-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b344",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 292,
      "bookHadithIndex": 144,
      "text": "Wa'il bin Hujr said:\"I arrived in Al-Madinah and I said, 'Let me look at the Salat of Allah's Messenger.' When he sat - meaning for At-Tashah-hud - he spread his left foot, and placed his left hand - meaning on his left thigh - and held his right foot erect",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-292-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-292-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-292-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-292-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b345",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 293,
      "bookHadithIndex": 145,
      "text": "Abbas bin SAhl [bin Sa'd] narrated:\"Abu Humaid, Abu Usaid, Sahl bin Sa'd, and Muhammad bin Maslamah were once together and they were mentioning the Salat of Allah's Messenger. Abu Humaid said: \"I am the most knowledgeable among you of the Salat of Allah's Messenger: Indeed Allah's Messenger sat - meaning for Tashah-hud - he spread his left foot, and made the top of his right (foot) face the Qiblah, and he placed his right hand on his right knee, and his left hand on his left knee, and indicated with his finger - meaning the index finge",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-293-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-293-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-293-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-293-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b346",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 294,
      "bookHadithIndex": 146,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated:\"When the Prophet would sit during the Salat, he would place his right hand on his knee, and raise his finger, the one that is next to the [right] thumb, supplicating with it, and his left hand was spread flat on his left knee",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-294-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-294-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-294-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b347",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 295,
      "bookHadithIndex": 147,
      "text": "Abdullah narrated:\"The Prophet would say the Salam from his right and from his left (saying): (As-Salamu alaikum wa rahmatullah, as-Salamu alaikum wa rahmatullah) 'Peace be upon you, and Allah's mercy. Peace be upon you, and Allah's mercy",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-295-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-295-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-295-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-295-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b348",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 296,
      "bookHadithIndex": 148,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"Allah's Messenger would say one Taslim for the Salat while facing forward and turning to his right side a little",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-296-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-296-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-296-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b349",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 297,
      "bookHadithIndex": 149,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated:\"Hadhf the Salam is a Sunnah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-297-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-297-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-297-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b34a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 2,
      "hadithIndex": 298,
      "bookHadithIndex": 150,
      "text": "Aishah narrated:\"When Allah's Messenger said the Salam he would not remain seated except long enough to say: (Allahumma antas-salam, wa minkas-salam, tabarakta dhal jalali wal-Ikram) 'O Allah! You are the One free of defects, and perfection is from You. Blessed are You, Possessor of Majesty and Honor",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-298-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-298-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-2-298-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}